    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "1." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Answers must be contextualised and grounded in cited sources.  3.2 Drafting assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk100> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, the company's are compliant with SecNumCloud at the hosting layer through the company's partnership with OuraneCloud, ensuring sovereign hosting of confidential data within EU." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk101> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding GDPR compliance, the company's are familiar with professional secrecy requirements and have experience working with clients bound by such obligations, including a national professional order. the company's also comply with anti-money laundering and combating the financing of terrorism (LCB-FT) obligations and understand the importance of not undermining a firm's reporting obligations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk102> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For data protection measures, the company's implement encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, with key management handled through the company's EU-based infrastructure. the company's also practice strict partitioning of client files with logical isolation per client and per mission, ensuring access controls prevent any cross-client circulation of data." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk103> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Pseudonymisation is used where relevant, and the company's adhere to data minimisation principles. the company's retention policies are configurable and aligned with legal archival obligations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk104> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of security controls, the company's Secure Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) includes code review, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing conducted by an external provider equivalent to CREST level. the company's have a vulnerability management process in place with remediation SLAs based on severity and an incident response plan that includes detection, notification, and remediation, aligning with the 72-hour GDPR breach-notification workflow. the company's audit logging capabilities include logging of access and every system output, and the company's have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed. the company's maintain a data processing register and have a Data Processing Agreement (DPA) available, aligned with GDPR Article 28." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk105> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For explainability and auditability, the company's product, Atelier, is grounded in sources, allowing for retrieval trace, audit log, and figure source linking. grounded supports internal quality control and statutory audit review, ensuring no ungrounded numeric output is produced." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk106> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given these capabilities and experiences, the company's can ensure compliance with the client's requirements regarding confidentiality, professional secrecy, GDPR compliance, encryption, pseudonymisation, and data hosting on secure infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk107> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires compliance with anti-money laundering obligations LCB-FT (con:con50), professional secrecy and confidentiality of client data (con:con34), auditor's independence and separation of duties (con:con48), and personal data protection GDPR (con:con36, con:con37)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk108> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What are the company's legal standing, procurement experience across EU jurisdictions, IP model, insurance, standard contractual clauses, and AI regulatory posture that can ensure compliance with these requirements? the company's is a Société par actions simplifiée (SAS) registered in France, with the company's registered office in Paris. the company's legal standing is up to date, with all social and fiscal obligations met." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk109> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for procurement experience, the company's has worked with private firms, regulated professions, and public-sector clients, which includes experience with contractual terms such as service levels, penalties, reversibility, audit rights, and confidentiality undertakings." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Assistance in drafting client letters and correspondence, mission notes, file memos and syntheses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk110> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding intellectual property, the Atelier platform is proprietary software owned by the company's, licensed to clients under a subscription or usage model for the contract term. the company's uses open-source components under permissive licenses and provides a Software Bill of Materials (SBOM) to clients." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk111> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, the company's AI models are used under Faber IA's AI models respective licenses, including a sovereign European open-weight model. the company's has professional liability insurance covering up to 10 million euros per claim, as well as general civil liability cover. the company's can provide certificates for professional liability insurance covering up to 10 million euros per claim, as well as general civil liability cover upon request." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk112> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of standard contractual clauses, the company's is familiar with the expectations of clients bound by professional secrecy and can incorporate relevant confidentiality undertakings into contracts." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk113> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for regulatory compliance, the company's maintains the company's obligations through a Security & Compliance function, focusing on professional-services deployment. the company's monitors obligations such as GDPR (including Article 28 processing agreements), professional secrecy, anti-money laundering framework (LCB-FT), auditor-independence and separation-of-duties rules for statutory audit, legal retention obligations for accounting documents, and emerging EU AI Act requirements. the company's ensures that the company's contractual framework does not compromise the company's professional obligations. the company's can provide administrative attestations as needed, including those related to the company's legal standing and compliance with regulatory requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk114> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In relation to data protection, the company's complies with GDPR requirements for client and employee personal data." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk115> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Client data is hosted in EU, and the company's does not transfer data outside EU." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk116> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Sensitive data is protected through encryption and pseudonymisation where relevant." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk117> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, the company's legal standing, procurement experience, IP model, insurance coverage, standard contractual clauses, and regulatory compliance posture are designed to ensure that the company's can meet the requirements related to anti-money laundering obligations, professional secrecy, auditor's independence, and personal data protection as specified in The tender." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk118> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client has a budget of 220000 over 3 years (con:con66), with annual operating costs to be controlled (req:req72)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk119> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimisation strategies our can propose?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution does not autonomously produce binding or signed deliverables; the professional validates.  3.3 Client-file handling support." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk120> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on our context, the reference budget for a project like this contract is 220000 euros over 3 years, which fits within our normal deal range and financial capacity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk121> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The annual revenue of our is 6200000 euros, with a near break-even result, indicating that our has a good financial foundation to take on projects like this contract." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk122> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the budget envelope for this contract, with one-off project costs estimated at 40% of the total budget (88000 euros) and recurring run costs at 60% (132000 euros) over 3 years, our target gross margin is between 25% and 35%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk123> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To achieve our target gross margin, our can propose cost-optimisation strategies such as favouring cost-efficient tiers or models for the solution, ensuring that the chosen configuration protects our target gross margin while preserving an acceptable level of service quality." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk124> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, maintaining a three-year cost model that can be adjusted if requirements or budgets change will help in controlling costs and optimising resources." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk125> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It's also important to note that our approach favours cost-efficient solutions that maintain predictability of recurring costs, which aligns with the client's requirement to control annual operating costs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk126> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By working closely with the client to understand the client needs and preferences, our can propose a tailored solution that meets the client budget constraints while achieving our target gross margin." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk127> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires a non-decisional support tool (con:con9) that improves productivity, quality, and reliability of work (req:req10), with contextualised answers grounded in cited sources (con:con23)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk128> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What are the company's LLM stack, RAG capabilities, fine-tuning methods, explainability tools, performance benchmarks, past AI use cases, and known trade-offs that can help the company's meet these requirements? the company's, has a platform called Atelier. the company's have a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, which allows every answer to be generated from passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus and cites passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus. the company's RAG capabilities include hybrid retrieval, re-ranking, query reformulation, multi-document synthesis, structured extraction with source linking, and template-guided drafting. the company's can provide contextualised answers grounded in cited sources, as the company's core approach is based on Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG). provide means that every answer is generated from passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus and cites passages retrieved from the client's controlled corpus." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk129> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our RAG capabilities include multi-document synthesis and structured extraction with source linking, which enable the company's to provide reliable and trustworthy answers. the company's explainability tools feature source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval trace, and every interaction logged for a posteriori audit. feature allows the company's to provide transparent and explainable results, which is essential for meeting the client's requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "During the handling and review of a client file, the solution must surface relevant information, recall applicable rules, propose a checklist of verifications and flag potential anomalies for human review (e.g. during the révision des comptes). the solution must support the preparation of recurring documents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk130> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of performance benchmarks, the company's measure answer quality using a labelled evaluation set built with the client, focusing on groundedness, relevance, factual support, and correctness of cited figures. the company's past AI use cases include delivering a regulatory-information assistant for a national professional order, a claims-handling assistant for a mutual health insurer, and a social-services case-work assistant for a regional council." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk131> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding fine-tuning methods, optional fine-tuning is technically available, but data use terms are defined with the firm and the compliance function before any such use. the company's also have model options, including a Sovereign European open-weight model (self-hosted) and top-tier proprietary models (via API), which can be chosen based on the client's specific requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk132> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for trade-offs, the company's model selection principle involves trading performance against explainability and sovereignty, made per engagement. trading means that the company's can choose the most suitable model based on the client's needs, balancing performance with the need for transparency and control." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk133> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, the company's capabilities, RAG approach, and explainability tools are well-suited to meet the client's requirements for a non-decisional support tool that improves productivity, quality, and reliability of work, with contextualised answers grounded in cited sources." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk134> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client wishes to limit environmental footprint of the solution (con:con70) and relies on low-carbon infrastructure (con:con71)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk135> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What are the company's EcoVadis rating, carbon footprint, green hosting partners, digital sobriety practices, social commitments, AI ethics principles, and known sustainability trade-offs that can help the company's meet these requirements? the company's, has an EcoVadis rating of Silver. the company's have conducted a bilan carbone assessment and have published a trajectory to reduce the company's carbon intensity per managed assistant year on year, covering scopes 1, 2, and main scope 3 items, including cloud inference.  the company's partner with green hosting providers, such as OuraneCloud in the EU region, which offers sovereign hosting, renewable energy, a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, and heat reuse. the company's also practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk136> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of social commitments, the company's are a signatory to the responsible tech charter, have objectives for gender balance and inclusion, and offer an apprenticeship and work-study program. the company's are also part of the Grenoble research ecosystem. the company's AI ethics principles include human oversight, transparency and source grounding, bias monitoring, data minimisation, and a documented data-use policy, all of which are aligned with the EU AI Act and have been reviewed by the company's compliance team." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk137> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding known sustainability trade-offs, the company's acknowledge the tension between our premium tier's energy intensity and our premium tier's associated footprint, ensuring that the trade-off is explicit." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk138> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "These capabilities and commitments can help meet the client's requirements for limiting environmental footprint and relying on low-carbon infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk139> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company proposes a tailored solution that meets Cabinet Vauclair Associés' requirements and constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "No decision or sign-off may be automated.  3.4 Collaboration and mission continuity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk140> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company understand that Our company has 250 staff, including chartered accountants, statutory auditors, accounting, payroll, and legal collaborators, and operates in the Belval region." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk141> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company must work with a large volume of regulatory and methodological reference material, including accounting standards, tax doctrine, the commercial code, collective bargaining agreements for payroll, internal procedures, and methodology guides. a tailored solution that meets Cabinet Vauclair Associés' requirements and constraints is designed to provide an intelligent assistance tool that supports Our company professionals in the firm's professionals daily activities, including retrieval of regulatory and methodological information, assistance in drafting professional documents, support in handling client files, and continuity of missions between collaborators. a tailored solution that meets Cabinet Vauclair Associés' requirements and constraints will be accessible from the firm's professionals work environment and will ensure strict respect for professional secrecy and confidentiality of client data." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk142> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company propose a hybrid agile iterations phase gate methodology, which includes framing, design, pilot, generalization, and run phases." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk143> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company approach optimizes costs, and Our company guarantee the expected quality of service." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk144> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company will provide change management support and training to ensure a smooth transition. a tailored solution that meets Cabinet Vauclair Associés' requirements and constraints integrates with Cabinet Vauclair Associés' production tools, including accounting production software, payroll software, and document management (GED)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk145> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company also integrate with the electronic invoicing dematerialization environment and user directory SSO." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk146> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company API-type interface ensures interoperability, and Our company guarantee confidentiality and security, respecting professional secrecy and auditor independence." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk147> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company comply with all relevant regulations, including GDPR, anti-money laundering obligations (LCB/FT), and auditor independence and separation of duties rules for statutory audit missions." ;
